  "question": {
    "text": "To get three images of a single object, one should have two plane mirrors at an angle of"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$60^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$90^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$120^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$30^{\\circ}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to Image formula\n$\\mathrm{n}=\\frac{360}{\\theta}-1 \\Rightarrow 3=\\frac{360}{\\theta}-1$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{360}{\\theta}=4 \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\frac{360}{4}=90$"
  }
